WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.716 --> 00:00:16.518
was nearly summer and the weather was much warmer, but nobody at Patty's Place was smiling.

2
00:00:17.399 --> 00:00:22.881
It was exam time, and ahead were their final exams for the year and possibly their last exams

3
00:00:22.961 --> 00:00:30.764
ever! If they passed, Phil, Stella, Anne, and Priscilla would all be graduates of Redmond College and all

4
00:00:30.804 --> 00:00:32.805
holders of Bachelor of Arts degrees.

5
00:00:32.825 --> 00:00:38.568
"I wish I were dead, or that it was tomorrow night," groaned Phil.

6
00:00:38.588 --> 00:00:43.790
"If you live long enough, both wishes will come true," said Anne calmly.

7
00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:47.371
"It's easy for you to be calm," said Phil.

8
00:00:47.391 --> 00:00:49.492
"You can do philosophy.

9
00:00:49.512 --> 00:00:51.053
I can't!

10
00:00:51.733 --> 00:00:55.315
And when I think of that horrible exam tomorrow, I get so nervous."

11
00:00:55.335 --> 00:00:57.576
"You won't fail.

12
00:00:58.504 --> 00:01:00.365
How did you do in your Greek exam today?"

13
00:01:00.745 --> 00:01:01.306
Anne asked.

14
00:01:01.326 --> 00:01:03.667
"I have no idea!

15
00:01:03.687 --> 00:01:06.448
I've studied so much I can't think anymore!"

16
00:01:06.889 --> 00:01:07.449
said Phil.

17
00:01:08.389 --> 00:01:15.273
The busy days flew by, and when the examinations were over, Anne got first-class honors in English, Priscilla

18
00:01:15.313 --> 00:01:18.475
got honors in classics, and Phil got honors in math.

19
00:01:20.996 --> 00:01:25.218
On graduation day Marilla proudly attended the ceremony in Halifax.

20
00:01:26.879 --> 00:01:30.717
After Marilla left, Anne went home to Patty's Place to begin packing.

21
00:01:30.737 --> 00:01:35.398
"Just imagine, in one week, I'll be in Avonlea!

22
00:01:36.218 --> 00:01:37.239
How delightful!"

23
00:01:37.559 --> 00:01:41.880
thought Anne, bending over the box in which she was packing her clothes and belongings.

24
00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:47.782
"But imagine, in one week, I'll be gone forever from Patty's Place.

25
00:01:48.642 --> 00:01:49.662
How horrible!"

26
00:01:51.663 --> 00:01:54.684
Actually, Anne wasn't sure what the future held for her.

27
00:01:55.596 --> 00:02:00.160
If Roy proposed to her, everything would change, and he would definitely propose to her soon.

28
00:02:01.141 --> 00:02:03.563
Anne felt that she was truly in love with Roy.

29
00:02:04.403 --> 00:02:09.007
It was not exactly as she had imagined love to be, she admitted to herself, but Roy was

30
00:02:09.047 --> 00:02:11.409
a good man, and they would be happy together.

31
00:02:11.429 --> 00:02:15.532
"Is anything in life really the way you imagine it to be?"

32
00:02:15.913 --> 00:02:16.593
wondered Anne.

33
00:02:18.014 --> 00:02:22.018
That evening, when Roy came to Patty's Place and asked Anne to go for a walk in the

34
00:02:22.038 --> 00:02:24.460
park, everyone at Patty's Place knew why.

35
00:02:25.416 --> 00:02:27.618
And they thought they knew what Anne's answer would be.

36
00:02:27.638 --> 00:02:30.760
"Anne's a lucky girl," said Phil.

37
00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:34.963
"I suppose so," said Stella, shrugging her shoulders.

38
00:02:34.983 --> 00:02:39.966
"Roy is a nice fellow, but there doesn't seem to be too much in him."

39
00:02:39.986 --> 00:02:42.828
"Stella! Why do you say that?"

40
00:02:43.188 --> 00:02:43.969
demanded Phil.

41
00:02:43.989 --> 00:02:51.314
"I'm not being nasty; it's just that I worry Anne may end up unhappy," Stella explained.

42
00:02:52.515 --> 00:02:58.530
Under an old oak tree in the park—a very romantic spot—Roy asked Anne to marry him.

43
00:02:59.311 --> 00:03:03.753
His proposal was perfectly worded, as if he had copied it from a book, but it was also

44
00:03:03.833 --> 00:03:05.174
heartfelt and sincere.

45
00:03:06.074 --> 00:03:08.436
Anne felt that she ought to be thrilled from head to foot.

46
00:03:09.236 --> 00:03:12.018
But she wasn't; she just felt numb.

47
00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:17.621
Anne opened her mouth to say "yes," and then, suddenly, found herself trembling.

48
00:03:18.981 --> 00:03:23.304
She felt as if she were looking over a cliff, and then she had a moment of revelation.

49
00:03:24.064 --> 00:03:25.905
Quickly, she pulled her hand from Roy's.

50
00:03:26.986 --> 00:03:32.909
"Oh, Roy, I can't marry you I can't I can't," Anne cried.

51
00:03:33.869 --> 00:03:34.910
Roy turned pale.

52
00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:36.731
"What do you mean?"

53
00:03:36.751 --> 00:03:41.954
"I thought I could marry you, but I can't," said Anne desperately.

54
00:03:41.974 --> 00:03:43.995
"Why can't you?"

55
00:03:44.475 --> 00:03:45.716
Roy asked more calmly.

56
00:03:45.736 --> 00:03:50.999
"Because said Anne, "I don't care enough for you."

57
00:03:51.819 --> 00:03:53.120
Roy's face changed.

58
00:03:53.968 --> 00:03:58.049
"So you've just been amusing yourself with my affections this past year?"

59
00:03:58.409 --> 00:03:59.250
he asked slowly.

60
00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:03.391
"No, no, I haven't," gasped Anne.

61
00:04:04.211 --> 00:04:05.511
Oh, how could she explain?

62
00:04:06.271 --> 00:04:07.292
She couldn't explain.

63
00:04:07.312 --> 00:04:10.353
"Forgive me, Roy," Anne pleaded.

64
00:04:10.373 --> 00:04:12.873
"I did think I cared.

65
00:04:13.673 --> 00:04:14.614
Really, I did.

66
00:04:15.394 --> 00:04:17.194
But I know now that I don't."

67
00:04:18.035 --> 00:04:19.095
She looked at the ground.

68
00:04:19.115 --> 00:04:25.754
"You are not the woman I thought you were," said Roy angrily, and then with a bitter tone,

69
00:04:25.774 --> 00:04:28.756
"You are the only woman I can ever love.

70
00:04:29.696 --> 00:04:30.937
You've ruined my life.

71
00:04:31.457 --> 00:04:32.438
Good-bye, Anne."

72
00:04:33.198 --> 00:04:33.959
He stormed off.

73
00:04:33.979 --> 00:04:40.143
"Good bye," Anne stammered too quietly for him to hear.

74
00:04:41.063 --> 00:04:44.485
She sat in the park, feeling drenched in shame and contempt.

75
00:04:46.126 --> 00:04:48.568
Anne slipped into Patty's Place and ran to her room.

76
00:04:49.592 --> 00:04:54.874
"I hope that no one will ever again ask me to get married as long as I live,"

77
00:04:55.355 --> 00:04:56.035
she sobbed.

78
00:04:56.955 --> 00:04:58.756
Phil heard her crying and came in.

79
00:05:02.758 --> 00:05:07.220
said Anne, "Roy asked me to marry him─and I refused."

80
00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.201
Her face was red with tears and shame.

81
00:05:10.221 --> 00:05:13.482
"You you refused Roy?"

82
00:05:13.963 --> 00:05:14.963
said Phil blankly.

83
00:05:14.983 --> 00:05:16.664
"Are you crazy?"

84
00:05:18.884 --> 00:05:21.745
"Oh, Phil, don't scold me," Anne pleaded.

85
00:05:21.765 --> 00:05:27.888
"I honestly thought I cared, but at the last minute I realized I couldn't do it."

86
00:05:27.908 --> 00:05:31.649
"Well, Anne, I think you've treated Roy badly.

87
00:05:31.669 --> 00:05:34.310
You've been seeing him for a whole year!"

88
00:05:34.791 --> 00:05:36.271
said Phil in exasperation.

89
00:05:37.151 --> 00:05:39.692
Anne nodded, embarrassed, and started to cry again.

90
00:05:40.533 --> 00:05:43.294
The two stayed up talking until they both felt better.

91
00:05:44.674 --> 00:05:48.076
The next day all the friends at Patty's Place said tearful good-byes.

92
00:05:49.012 --> 00:05:53.595
Priscilla and Stella were glad that Anne had not accepted Roy's proposal and told her so.

93
00:05:54.476 --> 00:05:55.577
Anne felt slightly better.

94
00:05:56.517 --> 00:06:01.521
All the girls hugged each other, made promises to see each other again as soon as possible, and

95
00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:04.043
caught the train or ferry to their respective homes.

96
00:06:05.784 --> 00:06:10.287
When Anne returned to Green Gables the next day, everything was as it had always been.

97
00:06:11.148 --> 00:06:12.869
At dinner Marilla, Mrs.

98
00:06:12.949 --> 00:06:18.252
Lynde, Davy, and Dora caught up on all of Anne's life and filled Anne in on what had

99
00:06:18.292 --> 00:06:19.253
happened in Avonlea.

100
00:06:20.073 --> 00:06:25.094
They talked about who had gotten married, how the weather had been, and how the spring harvest had

101
00:06:25.114 --> 00:06:25.635
turned out.

102
00:06:27.035 --> 00:06:32.817
There was a short silence, and suddenly Davy remarked, "Hey, Anne, did you know Gilbert Blythe is dying?"

103
00:06:32.837 --> 00:06:35.317
"Davy, hold your tongue!"

104
00:06:35.777 --> 00:06:36.257
said Mrs.

105
00:06:36.317 --> 00:06:37.118
Lynde angrily.

106
00:06:37.138 --> 00:06:39.258
"Anne, don't look like that!

107
00:06:40.019 --> 00:06:42.019
We didn't mean to tell you so suddenly."

108
00:06:42.039 --> 00:06:44.960
"Is it true?"

109
00:06:45.372 --> 00:06:47.313
asked Anne in a voice that was not hers.

110
00:06:48.253 --> 00:06:51.314
Her face was so white that Marilla feared Anne was going to faint.

111
00:06:51.334 --> 00:06:55.575
"Gilbert is very ill," said Mrs.

112
00:06:55.655 --> 00:06:56.455
Lynde gravely.

113
00:06:56.475 --> 00:07:00.016
"He caught typhoid fever just after he arrived.

114
00:07:00.836 --> 00:07:02.177
It doesn't look good."

115
00:07:03.197 --> 00:07:08.238
Anne walked blindly across the kitchen, through the hall, and up the stairs to her old room.

116
00:07:09.218 --> 00:07:12.359
At its window she knelt down, staring ahead without seeing.

117
00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.580
The sky was very dark.

118
00:07:15.429 --> 00:07:17.856
Rain was beating down on the shivering fields.

119
00:07:18.719 --> 00:07:20.525
And Gilbert was dying
